# Purpose

Next.js app to browse and match spiritual/intentional communities (monasteries, temples, zen centers, retreat centers, etc.) using Supabase data produced by the separate agent-system repo.

# Rules

- Follow `README.md` for architecture and setup; `docs/DATABASE.md` for Supabase/jsonb.
- When changing types, queries, matching, APIs, scripts, or env vars listed in `.cursor/rules/readme-sync.mdc`, update the relevant doc in the same change.

# References

- `README.md` — app docs, setup, matching summary
- `docs/DATABASE.md` — tables, jsonb schemas, queries
- [Agent system](https://github.com/meredithvf/monastery-finder-agent-system) — enrichment pipeline, DDL
- `src/lib/types/community.ts` — TypeScript mirrors of `profile` and `feature_scores` jsonb

